Let me redo the Taylor expansion more carefully.

f(t) = (1+3t+2t^2)^{1/t}
g(t) = (1+3t-2t^2)^{1/t}

Now continuing with the expansion:

f(t) = e^{3 - t/2 + 3t² - 17t³/4 + ...} = e³ · e^{-t/2 + 3t² - 17t³/4 + ...}
g(t) = e^{3 - 13t/2 + 15t² - 161t³/4 + ...} = e³ · e^{-13t/2 + 15t² - 161t³/4 + ...}
